        "original_id": "c101c1ac-8c21-5448-8549-9c47afbe87c3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tia Carrere, Jon Lovitz, Mekhi Phifer, Louise Fletcher, Malinda Williams, Brian Hooks\n- Works: High School High, General Hospital, All Day, All Night, High School High Soundtrack, A Low Down Dirty Shame (soundtrack), White Man's Burden (soundtrack), Space Jam (soundtrack)\n- Places: Los Angeles, California\n- Topics: film release dates, soundtrack appearances, acting careers\n\nFacts:\n- Tia Carrere, born Althea Rae Janairo on January 2, 1967, is an American actress, model, voice actress, and singer.\n- Tia Carrere obtained her first big break as a regular on the daytime soap opera General Hospital.\n- A Low Down Dirty Shame (soundtrack) included an appearance by the group in 1994 before the release of All Day, All Night.\n- White Man's Burden (soundtrack) included an appearance by the group in 1995 before the release of All Day, All Night.\n- High School High is a 1996 comedy film about an inner-city high school in the Los Angeles, California area.\n- High School High stars Jon Lovitz, Tia Carrere, Mekhi Phifer, Louise Fletcher, Malinda Williams, and Brian Hooks.\n- High School High Soundtrack and Space Jam (soundtrack) included appearances by the group in 1996 before the release of All Day, All Night.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6a4ed9dd-e844-5bea-b11f-43da39a0e5d3",
